# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Grenjo AI Tool - example environment file
#
# This application reads almost nothing from the environment, by design:
#
#   * no API keys       - they are entered in the UI and stored in the Windows
#                         credential store (DPAPI), never in a file;
#   * no server config  - there is no server;
#   * no database URL   - the database is a local SQLite file;
#   * no feature flags  - nothing here toggles behaviour.
#
# A desktop app that reads keys or endpoints from env invites them into shell
# history, CI logs and screenshots, so the app deliberately does not.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` only if you actually need one of the two development
# variables below. `.env` is gitignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where `npm run icon` writes its per-size PNG previews (optional; the script
# also writes build/icon.png, build/icon.ico and build/icon.icns regardless).
# ICON_PREVIEW_DIR=.work/icon-preview

# The dev renderer URL is set by `scripts/dev.mjs` itself when it starts Vite;
# setting it by hand is only useful when attaching to a server someone else runs.
# VITE_DEV_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5273
